@defgroup micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-operators Operators
@brief Deprecated overloaded operators for test comparisons.

@details
The `mt::operators` namespace defines the comparison operators `==`,
`!=`, `<`, `>`, `<=`, and `>=`, and the logical operators `and`, `or`, and
`not`, for the framework expression types. After
`using namespace mt::operators`, a check such as
`t.expect (mt::to_i{ compute_answer () } == 42_i)` reports the values of
its operands, as the function comparators do.

@par Deprecated
The operators are deprecated since 6.0.0, in favour of the function
comparators `mt::eq()`, `mt::ne()`, `mt::lt()`, `mt::le()`, `mt::gt()`,
and `mt::ge()`, and of the logical functions `mt::all_of()`,
`mt::any_of()`, and `mt::negate()`, which check and report the plain
values, without literal suffixes or wrappers.

@par Limitations
- The operators apply only when at least one operand is a framework
  expression type (see `extension::is_op`): a deprecated literal, such as
  `1_i`, or a deprecated wrapper, such as `mt::to_i{ value }`. When
  neither operand is, the standard operator is selected; it returns a plain
  `bool`, so a failed check cannot show the operands.
- The overloaded `and` and `or` operators evaluate both operands before
  the check, so they do not short-circuit like the built-in ones.

@par Replacement

@code{.cpp}
namespace mt = micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus;

ts.test ("Comparators", [] (auto& t) {
  t.expect (mt::eq (compute_answer (), 42)) << "answer is 42";
  t.expect (mt::ne (compute_answer (), 43)) << "answer is not 43";
  t.expect (mt::lt (compute_answer (), 43)) << "answer is < 43";
  t.expect (mt::le (compute_answer (), 43)) << "answer is <= 43";
  t.expect (mt::gt (compute_answer (), 41)) << "answer is > 41";
  t.expect (mt::ge (compute_answer (), 42)) << "answer is >= 42";
  t.expect (mt::all_of (mt::eq (compute_answer (), 42),
                        mt::eq (compute_float (), 42.0f)));
});
@endcode
